cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "eudr-geojson-validator: a conformance checker for EUDR geolocation files"
abstract: >-
  Checks a GeoJSON file against the European Commission's EUDR GeoJSON File
  Description, the format in which the geolocation of commodity plots is
  submitted under Regulation (EU) 2023/1115, and against the Regulation's
  definition of geolocation in Article 2(28). Errors (breaches of the
  specification) are kept apart from warnings (files that conform and are
  still probably wrong, such as coordinates entered latitude-first). A
  command-line tool and Python package with no runtime dependencies beyond
  the standard library, and a browser demo that runs the same code locally.
  It does not assess deforestation or compliance, and it is not legal advice.
authors:
  - family-names: Olagoke
    given-names: Adewole
repository-code: "https://github.com/aolagoke-dsae/eudr-geojson-validator"
url: "https://aolagoke-dsae.github.io/eudr-geojson-validator/"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/eudr-geojson-validator/"
license: MIT
version: "1.3.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
keywords:
  - EUDR
  - GeoJSON
  - deforestation
  - geolocation
  - validation
  - due diligence
references:
  - type: legal-rule
    title: >-
      Regulation (EU) 2023/1115 of the European Parliament and of the Council
      of 31 May 2023 on the making available on the Union market and the
      export from the Union of certain commodities and products associated
      with deforestation and forest degradation
    authors:
      - name: European Parliament and Council of the European Union
    year: 2023
    url: "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1115/oj"
  - type: manual
    title: "EUDR GeoJSON File Description, version 1.3 (EUDR Information System API reference)"
    authors:
      - name: European Commission
    year: 2026
    url: "https://eudr.webcloud.ec.europa.eu/tracesnt/help/eudr-documentation/operator/geojson-description.html"
    notes: "Followed where it differs from the PDF version 1.5 of 5 May 2025."
